#!/bin/sh
# tp: one command to drive the HP TouchPad hardware from a shell (BusyBox sh). Run `tp help`.
# It wraps the lower level helpers (charge-mode, wifi-wpa, bt-test, cpu-state ...) and the sysfs interfaces.
# the helpers are in /usr/local/bin, which callers such as daemons or CGIs may not have in their PATH
export PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:$PATH
P=/sys/class/power_supply

# system GPIO number of a PM8058 GPIO (1-based): the gpiochip of 44 lines
pmgpio() {
  for c in /sys/class/gpio/gpiochip*; do
    [ "$(cat $c/ngpio 2>/dev/null)" = 44 ] && { echo $(( $(cat $c/base) + $1 - 1 )); return; }
  done
}

usage() {
cat <<USAGE
tp info                      summary: kernel, battery, temperature, CPU, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth
tp battery                   battery and adapter details
tp charge [usb|750|900|1400|2000|status]   input current of the charger (default status)
tp power                     charge source, battery and the state of the power policy daemon
tp temp                      SoC temperature and thermal trips
tp cpu                       CPU and L2 clocks
tp backlight [on|off|0-100|status]   LCD backlight brightness in percent
tp wifi status|scan|connect <ssid>|wpa <ssid> <passphrase>|ps on|off|test [ssid]
tp bt up|psr|visible [s]|scan|status|down        Bluetooth controller (CSR BC6)
tp ssh                       show the SSH daemon and the addresses
tp panel open|close|toggle   settings panel in Cog (Alpine rootfs; triple Home runs toggle)
tp recovery                  reboot into the USB recovery mode
tp -j <command...>           JSON API of the settings panel (tp-panel, Alpine rootfs)
tp help
USAGE
}

# settings panel API: JSON output, kept apart so that the commands above stay human readable
[ "$1" = -j ] && { shift; command -v tp-panel > /dev/null || { echo '{"ok":false,"error":"no tp-panel"}'; exit 1; }; exec tp-panel "$@"; }

case "$1" in
  info)
    echo "kernel:  $(uname -r) ($(uname -v | cut -c1-40))  up $(cut -d. -f1 /proc/uptime) s"
    tp battery | head -2
    tp temp | grep -v trip | tr "
" " "; echo
    tp cpu | tr '\n' ' '; echo
    iw dev wlan0 link 2>/dev/null | grep -E "SSID|signal" | tr -d '\t' | tr '\n' ' '; echo
    ifconfig wlan0 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/.*inet addr:\([0-9.]*\).*/ip:      \1/p'
    echo "bt:      $(hcitool dev 2>/dev/null | tail -n +2 | tr -d '\t' | tr '\n' ' ')"
    ;;
  battery)
    echo "battery: $(cat $P/battery/capacity)%  $(( $(cat $P/battery/voltage_now) / 1000 )) mV  $(( $(cat $P/battery/current_now) / 1000 )) mA  $(( $(cat $P/battery/temp) / 10 )).$(( $(cat $P/battery/temp) % 10 )) C  $(cat $P/battery/status)  health $(cat $P/battery/health)"
    echo "adapter: online=$(cat $P/max8903_charger/online)  $(cat $P/max8903_charger/status)  health $(cat $P/max8903_charger/health)"
    ;;
  charge) shift; charge-mode "${1:-status}" ;;
  power)
    echo "udc: $(cat /sys/class/udc/*/state 2>/dev/null)  (not attached = wall adapter or nothing, configured = a PC)"
    charge-mode status
    echo "policy: $(cat /tmp/tp-powerd.state 2>/dev/null || echo 'daemon not running')"
    ;;
  temp)
    for z in /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*; do
      echo "$(cat $z/type): $(( $(cat $z/temp) / 1000 )) C"
      for t in $z/trip_point_*_temp; do [ -f "$t" ] && echo "  trip $(cat ${t%_temp}_type): $(( $(cat $t) / 1000 )) C"; done
    done
    ;;
  cpu) cpu-state ;;
  backlight)
    # brightness 0-100 through the pwm-backlight class device; falls back to the enable GPIO without the PWM driver
    B=/sys/class/backlight/backlight
    if [ -d $B ]; then
      MAX=$(cat $B/max_brightness)
      case "$2" in
        on)  echo $MAX > $B/brightness ;;
        off) echo 0 > $B/brightness ;;
        ""|status) ;;
        *[!0-9]*) echo "usage: tp backlight [on|off|0-100|status]"; exit 1 ;;
        *)   [ "$2" -le 100 ] || { echo "brightness is 0-100"; exit 1; }
             echo $(( ($2 * MAX + 50) / 100 )) > $B/brightness ;;
      esac
      echo "backlight: $(( ($(cat $B/brightness) * 100 + MAX / 2) / MAX )) % (level $(cat $B/brightness)/$MAX)"
    else
      N=$(pmgpio 25)
      [ -n "$N" ] || { echo "pm8058 gpio chip not found"; exit 1; }
      [ -d /sys/class/gpio/gpio$N ] || echo $N > /sys/class/gpio/export
      case "$2" in
        on)  echo out > /sys/class/gpio/gpio$N/direction; echo 1 > /sys/class/gpio/gpio$N/value ;;
        off) echo out > /sys/class/gpio/gpio$N/direction; echo 0 > /sys/class/gpio/gpio$N/value ;;
      esac
      echo "backlight enable (no PWM driver): $(cat /sys/class/gpio/gpio$N/value)"
    fi
    ;;
  wifi)
    case "$2" in
      status) iw dev wlan0 link; iw dev wlan0 get power_save; ifconfig wlan0 | sed -n 's/.*inet addr:\([0-9.]*\).*/ip \1/p' ;;
      scan)   ifconfig wlan0 up; iw dev wlan0 scan | awk '/^BSS/ {b=$2} /freq:/ {f=$2} /signal:/ {s=$2} /SSID:/ {sub(/^[ \t]*SSID: /,""); printf "%s dBm  %s MHz  %s\n", s, f, $0}' | sort -n -r | head -${3:-30} ;;
      connect) wifi-connect "$3" ;;
      wpa)     wifi-wpa "$3" "$4" ;;
      ps)      iw dev wlan0 set power_save "${3:-off}"; iw dev wlan0 get power_save ;;
      test)    wifi-selftest "${3:-AKTO-GUEST}" ;;
      *) usage ;;
    esac ;;
  bt)
    case "$2" in
      up)      bt-test 115200 bcsp noflow 2>&1 | tail -n 12; bt-psr 2>&1 | grep -v Loading | tail -n 8 ;;
      psr)     bt-psr ;;
      visible) bt-visible "${3:-60}" ;;
      scan)    hcitool -i hci0 scan --length=6 --flush ;;
      status)  hcitool dev; hcitool -i hci0 cmd 0x04 0x0001 | tail -n 2 ;;
      down)    killall hciattach 2>/dev/null; hciup 0 down 2>/dev/null ;;
      *) usage ;;
    esac ;;
  ssh) ps | grep "[d]ropbear"; ifconfig | sed -n 's/.*inet addr:\([0-9.]*\).*/ip \1/p' ;;
  panel)
    # Cog listens on the session bus started by /etc/tp.d/S90browser; /run/tp.panel marks the panel as shown
    command -v cogctl > /dev/null || { echo "panel: no cogctl (Alpine rootfs only)"; exit 1; }
    export DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/run/dbus-session
    A="$2"; [ "$A" = toggle ] && { [ -f /run/tp.panel ] && A=close || A=open; }
    case "$A" in
      open)  cogctl open http://127.0.0.1:8080/ && touch /run/tp.panel ;;
      close) U=about:blank; [ -s /mnt/media/touchpad/url ] && U=$(head -n1 /mnt/media/touchpad/url | tr -d '\r')
             cogctl open "$U" && rm -f /run/tp.panel ;;
      *) usage ;;
    esac ;;
  recovery) echo "rebooting into recovery"; devmem 0x2A05F65C 32 0x6f656d11; devmem 0x00800820 32 0 ;;
  help|"") usage ;;
  *) echo "unknown command: $1"; usage; exit 1 ;;
esac
